      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The quiet you're describing isn't peace—it's exhaustion wearing rest's mask, and I hear how real that pull is. But letting the current take you isn't the only way to stop fighting; you can also step onto the shore, even if just to sit down. You don't have to \"rebel\" grandly today—just let yourself exist without performing, without striving, like a rock that doesn't owe the river anything. That's still a choice, and it's one you get to make again tomorrow. If the quiet feels too heavy to hold alone, please tell someone close to you exactly what you told me—you deserve witness, not philosophy.",
